        "id": "F1",
        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "engine/runtime/ownerrules_block.go:245-249",
        "claim": "RemoveFile deletes any regular file whose content becomes empty after removal. A pre-existing, empty CLAUDE.md that install appended the block to is therefore deleted on uninstall rather than given back. The commit claims byte-exact restoration, and the file's existence is part of what the owner had. The Remove-level test covers the empty-content case but no file-level test does. The blockFile.existed flag is read but not used to tell an install-created file from an empty owner file.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/runtime/ownerrules_block.go:245-249",
          "engine/runtime/ownerrules_block_test.go: 'empty file' case exercises Remove only"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "F2",
        "severity": "SUGGESTION",
        "location": "engine/runtime/ownerrules.go:41-46",
        "claim": "Any locateOverlay error with an empty OverlayDir is mapped to ErrNoOverlayCheckout, not only 'no checkout found'. A different failure, such as the working directory being unreadable, is reported as the benign 'no overlay checkout' note with restart_required status instead of partial.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/runtime/ownerrules.go:41-46"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Traced Apply and Remove for LF, CRLF, no-final-newline and trailing-blank-line contents; they round-trip at the string level.",
      "The file-level RemoveFile path deletes any regular file whose updated content is empty, regardless of blockFile.existed, so an owner's empty file does not survive install then uninstall.",
      "The no-checkout path in claude.go returns restart_required with a note, and status returns supported without checking the block, as the commit message specifies."
